<pre class=metadata>
Title: Platform Media Query
Shortname: platform-media-query
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/CSS-Additions/system-media-queries/platform/spec/
Repository: arronei/CSS-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification adds the '@media/platform' media feature, which reports the family of the user's
    operating system from a closed list of keywords, so that a style sheet can follow that platform's
    conventions: writing a shortcut as ⌘K or Ctrl+K, ordering the buttons of a dialog, offering the right
    download, or showing the right app store badge. The value must be the same platform the user agent
    already reveals in its <code>User-Agent</code> header and, where it has them, its client hints, including
    when the user agent deliberately reports a platform it isn't running on, so the feature adds no
    information to any context. It never reports the version of the operating system, the device model, the
    architecture, or the browser.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css yes
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

